======================================================================
INVESTIGATION D: WHAT DISTINGUISHES H CLASSES? (n=7)
======================================================================

H class characteristics:
      H  count    c3    c5  comm_dim    tr(S^4)    tr(S^6)
    171   1680    14    36         7      486.0    -6090.0
    175    720    14    28         7      742.0   -14154.0
    189    240    14    42        19      294.0    -2058.0

Cycle counts are the DISCRIMINANT between iso-spectral classes.
Since tr(S^k) is the same for all (same eigenvalues),
the distinction must come from the eigenvector structure,
which is captured by the non-trace invariants of S^k.

